Windows
=======

Astir is not supported on Windows, and has never been built or run there.

This file used to carry Xastir's Cygwin instructions, written in 2017 for a
build that needed an X server and Motif.  Astir needs neither -- it is a GTK4
program and the Motif front end is not built -- so following those instructions
could only fail, and leaving them here would waste somebody's afternoon.

If you want to try it, the shape of the work is roughly:

  * MSYS2 with the UCRT64 toolchain, rather than Cygwin.  GTK4 is packaged
    there as mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gtk4.
  * The optional map libraries -- shapelib, PCRE2, GraphicsMagick, libcurl,
    libgeotiff, proj -- are packaged there too, under the same prefix.
  * Serial ports and AX.25 are the parts least likely to work unchanged.
    APRS-IS over TCP is the piece most likely to work first, and is the
    sensible thing to get running before anything else.

Nothing above has been tested.  It is a starting point, not a procedure.  If
you get it working, a report of what had to change would be worth more than
this file is.
